.TH EXP 3M
.SH NAME
exp, log, log10, pow, sqrt \- exponential, logarithm, power, square root
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <math.h>"
.sp
.B "double exp(x)"
.B "double x;"
.sp
.B "double log(x)"
.B "double x;"
.sp
.B "double log10(x)"
.B "double x;"
.sp
.B "double pow(x, y)"
.B "double x, y;"
.sp
.B "double sqrt(x)"
.B "double x;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B exp
returns the exponential function of
.IR x .
.PP
.B log
returns the natural logarithm of
.IR x ;
.B log10
returns the base 10 logarithm
of
.IR x .
.PP
.B pow
returns
.IR x ** y .
.PP
.B sqrt
returns the square root of
.IR x .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
hypot(3), sinh(3), intro(2)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B exp
and
.B pow
return a huge value when the correct value would overflow;
.B errno
is set to ERANGE.
.B pow
returns 0 and sets
.B errno
to EDOM when
the second argument is negative and non-integral or when both arguments
are 0.
.PP
.B log
returns 0 when
.I x
is zero or negative;
.B errno
is set to EDOM.
.PP
.B sqrt
returns 0 when
.I x
is negative;
.B errno
is set to EDOM.
.sp
